   "subject": "updateSelectInput does not reactively change label?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi there,<br><br>I am using Shiny to visualize some statistics. The UI has to be in multiple languages such that the entire context switches as the language selection is triggered. So this is what I am doing:<br><br>I have defined some named lists to store the texts in corresponding languages and I have defined the following select input and slider input fields in ui.R with initial values in a default language:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">selectInput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;clsLev&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> clsLevLabel$nl</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> levList$nl</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> levList$nl</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>sliderInput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;numRes&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> numResLabel$nl</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> min </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> max </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> value </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> step </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span></div></code></div><br>Language selection is also controlled by a select input field:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">selectInput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;lang&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> langLabel$nl</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;en&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;nl&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;fr&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;de&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;nl&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br>Accordingly, in server.R I defined an observer to update the two input fields when &quot;input$lang&quot; changes, as follows:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">observe</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    updateSelectInput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">session</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;clsLev&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> label </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> clsLevLabel</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input$lang</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]],</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> choices </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> levList</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input$lang</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    updateSliderInput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">session</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;numRes&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> label </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> numResLabel</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input$lang</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span></div></code></div><br>I think I am doing in a right way, however it is very strange that it works only partially: the label of the slider input and the choices of the select input change accordingly, but the label of the select input remains unchanged.<br><br>Is there anyone who has also encountered such kind of issue or am I doing it in a wrong way? Any comment or suggestion will be a great help for me. Thank you in advance.<br><br>Regards,<br>Yang<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
